From 8fc85c057935b800d5539384c85be950029fce22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:09:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! validation, net: split admission into reusable phases
 (no behavior change)

Recover the P2P context-free precompute from original input 05f65fad43,
whose net_processing.cpp hunks were dropped by the historical best-effort
construction of eCash 042 (maintained owner 59b352c43e). Keep the current
one-pass serial admission and relay/orphan/reject semantics, rather than
restoring the obsolete atomic ProcessRawTxBatch/fallback path.

Stage regular checks and the transaction-owned sighash cache outside
cs_main for serial bursts of at least eight transactions. Preserve receive
indices, including duplicates, malformed members and null slots; pass only
txid-bound context-free outcomes to ordinary admission. Script verification,
coin lookup, fee rules and commit ordering remain authoritative. The default
parallel admission thread already stages its own checks and is untouched.

This adapter belongs with ded34657ed, where PrecomputedAdmissionChecks and
ProcessSingleTx first exist; do not move those APIs into original owner 70.
Add slot/malformed tests and real Schnorr verdict parity with a bad signature
and mismatched precompute slots. Compilation and runtime tests await the
resource coordinator grant; this commit is source-complete, not validated.
---
 src/net_processing.cpp     | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/net_processing.h       | 10 ++++++
 src/test/txrelay_tests.cpp | 69 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 128 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/net_processing.cpp b/src/net_processing.cpp
